B13 types whose method-field graph splits
  rule: LCOM4 per type, over its self methods that are not accessors (an accessor touches exactly one field and nothing else): nodes are those methods (all impl blocks) and the fields; edges join a method to each field it reads or writes and to each self method it calls; a bare use of self joins every field
  limits: a method that touches no field and calls no self method is its own component; trait default bodies and fields reached through helpers are not seen
